window.AG_CHAPTERS["12"] = {"id":"12","title":"The Weaver's Winter Cough","titleZh":"織坊的冬咳","patient":{"name":"Auntie Qiu 邱嬸","sprite":"girl"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-clinic.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Lung and Spleen Qi Deficiency 肺脾氣虛","principle":"build earth to generate metal, and transform the phlegm","tongue":"pale body, white slippery coating","pulseNote":{"en":"Narrow and soft, and it gives way under the finger — there is very little push behind it.","zh":"細軟無力，按之即陷，鼓動甚微"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>F&#275;ngl&#243;ng ST40</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"ST40","zh":"豐隆","py":"F&#275;ngl&#243;ng","x":162,"y":552,"img":"art/body-leg-anterior.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":76,"y":300,"w":290,"h":480},"decoys":[{"x":180,"y":337},{"x":205,"y":552},{"x":150,"y":640},{"x":196,"y":452},{"x":172,"y":430}],"note":"<b>豐隆 F&#275;ngl&#243;ng ST40</b> — 8 cun below the knee, about midway between the knee crease and the tip of the outer ankle bone, roughly 1.5 cun lateral to the crest of the shin. Connecting point of the Stomach, and the principal point for transforming phlegm.<br>外膝眼下八寸，約當膝與外踝尖之中點，脛骨前緣外約一寸半。胃之絡穴，化痰之要穴。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"She has a cough and she has a poor appetite. Ask about both, and then ask which came first.","zh":"其人咳而納呆。二者俱問，且問孰先。"},"look":{"en":"Look at the colour, and then look at how <b>wet</b> the coating is. Fluid that is not being transformed has to sit somewhere.","zh":"觀其色，復觀其苔之潤否。水津不化，必有所停。"},"pulse":{"en":"Not enough blood to fill the vessel, and not enough qi to push it. Both are in this pulse.","zh":"血不充其道，氣不鼓其行。二者俱在此脈。"},"dx":{"en":"Are both organs weak? Then which of the five-element relations connects them? Then decide which one to treat.","zh":"二臟俱虛否？其五行之屬何關係？末定當治何臟。"},"rx":{"en":"Feed the mother and the child is fed. And something must be done about the phlegm that has already collected.","zh":"補其母則子受其養。且已聚之痰，不可不化。"},"tech":{"en":"Everything here is empty, and nothing here is hot. That combination permits something the last few patients did not.","zh":"通案皆虛，通案無熱。此二者並見，則前數案所不許者，於此可行。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen listens to her cough and does not react to it. \"Weak,\" he says. \"Note that.\"","zh":"參師父聽了她的咳，並不動容。「聲低，」他說，「記下。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"Auntie Qiu clears her throat and produces a great deal of thin white phlegm.","zh":"邱嬸清了清喉嚨，咯出許多稀白之痰。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy fetches a stool without being asked. She has been standing a while.","zh":"藥童不待吩咐就搬來凳子。她已站了好一會兒。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Twelve winters at the loom, and every winter this cough. It arrives with the cold and leaves in spring.\"","zh":"「織了十二個冬天，年年此咳。天寒則來，開春則去。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"I eat almost nothing now,\" she says. \"That started long before the cough did.\"","zh":"「現在幾乎吃不下，」她說，「這比咳嗽早得多。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"There. She has just told you which organ failed first. Do not lose that sentence.\"","zh":"「就是這句。她已告訴你何臟先病。莫失此語。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"excess_def","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"excess_def","dx":"channel_organ","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"cold_heat"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Build Earth to Generate Metal","cardZh":"培土生金","cardTxt":"Earth generates Metal, so the Spleen is the Lung's mother. When a long cough sits on a weak appetite, treating the Lung alone refills a cup with a hole in it. Strengthen the Spleen and the Lung is supplied from upstream — and the phlegm stops being made in the first place.","herbId":"dangshen","herbEn":"Codonopsis Root","herbZh":"黨參","herbImg":"art/card-dangshen.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sweet and neutral, entering Spleen and Lung — the two organs at fault here, in one herb. It tonifies the qi of both and generates fluids while it does so, and it is mild enough to stay in a formula for months, which a long illness needs."},"endings":{"three":["The following winter Auntie Qiu is at the loom through the cold months. \"I still cough in January,\" she says, \"but I eat, and it goes by itself.\"<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You treated the mother. Anyone can quiet a cough for a week — you stopped the thing that was making the phlegm.\"","次年冬天，邱嬸整個寒季都在織機前。「正月還是咳，」她說，「但吃得下，咳幾天自己就好了。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「你治其母。止一週之咳人人能之，你止的是生痰之源。」"],"two":["The cough loosens and the phlegm thins. Her appetite is still poor.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You helped the child. The mother is still hungry.\"","咳鬆了，痰也稀了，胃口仍差。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你顧了子。母猶未飽。」"],"one":["No change, and she is tired enough that the herb boy walks her home.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Which organ did she say failed first? She told you plainly. Go back and listen again.\"","未見好轉，且倦甚，藥童送她回去。<br><b>參師父：</b>「她說何臟先病？其言甚明。回去再聽一遍。」"],"titles":["Auntie Qiu Works the Winter","Auntie Qiu Coughs Less","Auntie Qiu Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Yesterday's pair was one organ pressing another. Today's pair is one organ feeding another.","cn":"昨日之對，一臟迫一臟；今日之對，一臟養一臟。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. Qiu. I work the looms. Every winter I cough, and every winter it lasts longer than the one before.","cn":"大夫。姓邱，織坊做工。年年冬咳，且一年長過一年。"},{"w":"patient","en":"There is a lot of phlegm, thin and white. And I am short of breath if I climb anything.","cn":"痰多，稀而色白。稍一登高就氣短。"},{"w":"master","en":"Cough, breathlessness, copious thin phlegm. That is the Lung. Now ask her about her table.","cn":"咳、氣短、痰多而稀，此肺也。今當問其飲食。"},{"w":"master","en":"Because in Chinese medicine the Lung does not make its own supply. Something upstream does.","cn":"蓋中醫謂肺不自生其氣，其源在上游。"}],"qa":[{"q":"How is your appetite, and how long has it been poor?","cq":"胃口如何？納呆幾時起？","good":1,"a":"Very small, and it has been that way for years — long before the cough started.","ca":"吃得極少，這樣已有數年，比咳嗽早得多。","clue":{"en":"Poor appetite, predating the cough by years","zh":"納呆數年，先於咳嗽"},"note":"<b>The single most important answer in the case.</b> It establishes the order: the Spleen failed first and the Lung followed. Order decides which organ you treat — and here it points upstream, to the mother. 本案最要之答。其序既定：脾先病而肺從之。序定則所治之臟定，而此指其上游，即其母也。"},{"q":"What does the phlegm look like, and is there much of it?","cq":"痰之色質如何？其量多寡？","good":1,"a":"A great deal, thin and white, and it comes up easily.","ca":"量多，稀白，易咯。","clue":{"en":"Copious thin white phlegm","zh":"痰多、稀白、易咯"},"note":"Thin and white is cold or damp phlegm, not heat. Copious and easily raised points at the Spleen rather than the Lung: 脾為生痰之源，肺為貯痰之器 — the Spleen is the source that makes phlegm, the Lung is only the vessel that stores it. 稀白者寒濕之痰，非熱。多而易咯者責之脾而不責之肺：「脾為生痰之源，肺為貯痰之器」。"},{"q":"What are your stools like, and do you feel heavy after eating?","cq":"大便如何？食後身重否？","good":1,"a":"Loose most days, and afterwards I want to sit down.","ca":"多半是溏的，飯後只想坐著。","clue":{"en":"Loose stool, heaviness after meals","zh":"便溏、食後困重"},"note":"The Spleen confirmed. Loose stool and post-meal heaviness are transformation failing — the same failure that is turning her fluids into phlegm instead of into qi. One mechanism, two symptoms, two organs. 脾證乃定。便溏、食後困重者，運化失職。其所以生痰者，亦此一失。一機而二症，而及二臟。"},{"q":"Do you have a fever, or thirst for cold drinks?","cq":"發熱嗎？渴喜冷飲嗎？","good":0,"a":"No. If anything I prefer warm water, and not much of it.","ca":"沒有。反而喜溫飲，也喝得不多。","clue":"","note":"A clean exclusion of heat — and it matters, because it decides whether moxa is allowed. Compare the ferryman in chapter eight: same cough, hot pattern, no moxa. 排除熱證，且關乎能否施灸。對比第八章之船家：咳同而證熱，故不灸。"},{"q":"Is it harder to breathe in than out, and is your low back sore?","cq":"吸難於呼否？腰痠嗎？","good":0,"a":"No, breathing out is the harder part. My back is fine.","ca":"不會，反倒是呼氣費力些。腰沒事。","clue":"","note":"An excellent exclusion, and a precise one. Difficulty <b>inhaling</b> with a sore low back would mean the Kidney is failing to grasp qi — a different pair entirely, Lung and Kidney rather than Lung and Spleen. 排除得極精。若吸氣為難而兼腰痠，則為腎不納氣，其對為肺腎而非肺脾。"}],"look":[{"t":"Pale body with a white slippery coating","c":"舌淡、苔白滑","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Pale tongue, white slippery coat","zh":"舌淡苔白滑"},"note":"Correct, and it reads as two organs at once. Pale = qi and blood are short. White = cold rather than heat. Slippery and wet = fluids sitting where they should have been transformed. That wetness is the phlegm, seen on the tongue before it is coughed up. 是，一舌而見二臟。淡者氣血不足，白者屬寒不屬熱，滑潤者水津停而未化。此潤即其痰，未咯而先見於舌。"},{"t":"Red body with a yellow greasy coat","c":"舌紅、苔黃膩","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm-heat — the ferryman of chapter eight. The phlegm is right; the temperature is the opposite. 痰熱之象，即第八章船家。痰是而寒熱適反。"},{"t":"Red body with little coating","c":"舌紅少苔","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat — the kiln master of chapter seven, whose cough was dry. Hers is drowning in phlegm. 陰虛內熱，即第七章窯場之乾咳。本案痰多，適與之反。"},{"t":"Pale body with a thin white coat and no moisture","c":"舌淡苔薄白而不潤","ok":0,"note":"That is simple qi deficiency without the fluid problem. Close, but it misses the wetness — and the wetness is where the phlegm is. 此為單純氣虛而水津未停。相近，然漏其潤，而潤處正痰之所在。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Thready and weak 細弱","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Thready weak pulse","zh":"脈細弱"},"note":"Correct. Thready: the vessel is under-filled. Weak: nothing is pushing hard. Both are deficiency, and neither has any force or heat in it — which fits a woman whose organs have been quietly failing for years rather than one fighting a pathogen. 是。細者脈道不充，弱者鼓動無力，二者皆虛，俱無力無熱。其人臟氣積年漸虧，非與邪相爭者，故脈如此。"},{"t":"Slippery and rapid 滑數","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm plus heat — the full pattern from chapter eight. Her phlegm is real but there is no heat and no force. 痰而兼熱，即第八章之實證。本案痰誠有之，然無熱亦無力。"},{"t":"Wiry 弦","ok":0,"note":"The Liver's pulse — yesterday's patient, not today's. Nothing here points at constraint. 肝之本脈，昨日之案，非今日之案。本案無鬱可指。"},{"t":"Floating and tight 浮緊","ok":0,"note":"Exterior wind-cold. This has been going on for twelve winters. 風寒表證。本病歷十二冬矣。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — are both organs weak, or only one?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：二臟俱虛，抑或一臟？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Both — the Lung and the Spleen","c":"二臟俱虛 — 肺與脾","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and each has its own evidence. <b>Lung:</b> chronic weak cough, breathlessness on exertion, copious phlegm, a quiet voice. <b>Spleen:</b> poor appetite for years, loose stool, heaviness after meals, a pale tongue. Neither list is empty and neither explains the other's findings on its own. 是，二者各有其憑。肺：久咳無力、動則氣短、痰多、聲低。脾：納呆積年、便溏、食後困重、舌淡。二者皆不空，且互不能相代。"},{"t":"Only the Lung","c":"獨在肺","ok":0,"note":"Then what accounts for years of poor appetite, loose stool and heaviness after eating? The Lung governs none of those. 若獨在肺，則納呆數年、便溏、食後困重何屬？此三者非肺所主。"},{"t":"Only the Spleen","c":"獨在脾","ok":0,"note":"Then what accounts for the cough, the breathlessness and the phlegm being coughed up? The Spleen makes phlegm but it does not cough. 若獨在脾，則咳、氣短、咯痰何屬？脾能生痰而不能咳。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — which five-element relation connects them?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：二臟之五行關係為何？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Mother and child — Earth generates Metal","c":"母子相生 — 土生金","ok":1,"note":"<b>Correct, and this is the whole reason the chapter exists.</b> The Spleen is Earth, the Lung is Metal, and Earth generates Metal — so the Spleen is the Lung's mother. When the mother cannot supply, the child goes hungry: 母病及子. Contrast yesterday's case, where Liver and Spleen were controller and controlled. Same two-organ shape, opposite ring. 是，本章之設，正為此理。脾屬土，肺屬金，土生金，故脾為肺之母。母不能供則子飢，是謂母病及子。對比昨日之案：肝脾為剋與被剋。同為二臟，而環不同。"},{"t":"Controller and controlled — Earth controls Water","c":"剋與被剋 — 土剋水","ok":0,"note":"Earth does control Water, but Water is the Kidney, not the Lung. Wrong pair. 土誠剋水，然水者腎也，非肺。所配非其人。"},{"t":"Insulting — Metal insulting Earth","c":"相侮 — 金侮土","ok":0,"note":"Insulting runs backwards along the <b>controlling</b> cycle, and Metal does not control Earth in the first place — Earth generates Metal. Wrong ring entirely. 相侮者逆剋道而行，且金本不剋土——土生金也。所循之環全非。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — so which organ do you treat?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：然則當治何臟？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Chiefly the Spleen — tonify the mother to treat the child","c":"主治脾 — 虛則補其母","ok":1,"note":"Correct: 培土生金, building earth to generate metal. Treating the Lung alone refills a cup with a hole in it — and it leaves the Spleen still making phlegm, which is why this cough returns every winter. Support the Lung too, by all means; but the weight of the prescription goes to the mother. 是，此謂培土生金。獨治其肺，如注水於漏杯；且脾仍生痰，故此咳年年而復。肺亦當顧，然方之所重在母。"},{"t":"Chiefly the Lung — treat where the symptoms are loudest","c":"主治肺 — 症之顯者治之","ok":0,"note":"Loudest is not the same as first. Treat where the symptoms are and she improves until the next cold snap; treat where they come from and the pattern stops repeating. 顯者未必先。治其所見，則遇寒復作；治其所自，則其證乃止。"},{"t":"Neither — wait for the season to change","c":"二者皆不治，俟其時令自轉","ok":0,"note":"It has changed twelve times and the cough has got longer each year. A pattern that worsens across seasons is not waiting to resolve. 時令已轉十二次，而其咳年長一年。逐年而重者，非待其自解。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"ST36","t":"Z&#250;s&#257;nl&#464; ST36 足三里","ok":1,"note":"The great tonifying point of the middle burner, and here it is the mother being fed. Spleen and Stomach are the source of acquired qi; strengthen them and the Lung is supplied from upstream. 補中焦之要穴，於此即補其母。脾胃為後天之本，補之則肺得其養於上游。"},{"id":"LU9","t":"T&#224;iyu&#257;n LU9 太淵","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Lung — the point for a Lung that is depleted rather than obstructed. It is also, by element, the Earth point of the Lung channel, which makes it the Lung's own mother point: tonifying earth without leaving the Lung channel. 肺之原穴，主肺之自虧而非邪阻。且以五行言，為肺經之土穴，即肺之母穴：不離本經而培其土。"},{"id":"ST40","t":"F&#275;ngl&#243;ng ST40 豐隆","ok":1,"note":"The principal point for transforming phlegm. Building the Spleen stops new phlegm being made; this clears what has already collected. Cause and consequence need separate points. 化痰之要穴。健脾者止其新生，此穴去其已聚。因與果，各需其穴。"},{"id":"LU10","t":"Y&#250;j&#236; LU10 魚際","ok":0,"note":"Spring point of the Lung — it clears heat. There is no heat here at all, and cooling an already cold, weak patient makes the phlegm harder to move. 肺之滎穴，主清熱。本案通身無熱，而寒虛者更清之，其痰益難行。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Y&#299;nl&#237;ngqu&#225;n SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Drains damp, and it drains. Damp is present, but it exists <i>because</i> the Spleen is too weak to move it — draining without building leaves the same Spleen making the same damp next week. 利濕而主瀉。濕誠有之，然其所以生者，脾虛不運耳。但利不建，則來週其濕如故。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"T&#224;ich&#333;ng LR3 太衝","ok":0,"note":"Yesterday's point, and yesterday's pattern. Nothing here is constrained — no wandering pain, no wiry pulse, no emotional trigger. 昨日之穴，昨日之證。本案無鬱：痛不走竄、脈不弦、不因情志而發。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method, with moxa","c":"補法，可施灸","ok":1,"note":"<b>Correct on both counts, and the moxa is the point.</b> Everything here is empty, so reinforce. And moxa warms and dries — which was forbidden for the kiln master (dry), forbidden for the ferryman (hot), and is exactly right here: a pale, cold, phlegm-damp patient with no heat anywhere in the case. Moxa at ST36 in particular is the classical treatment for this pattern. 二者皆是，而要義在灸。通案皆虛，故補。灸性溫燥：於窯場之燥者忌，於船家之熱者忌，於本案則正宜——面淡體寒、痰濕而通案無熱。足三里施灸，尤為本證古法。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, but no moxa","c":"補法，不施灸","ok":0,"note":"Cautious, and the caution is misplaced. Moxa is withheld for heat or dryness. She has neither, and cold damp phlegm is precisely what warmth moves. 其慎失所。忌灸者為熱為燥。本案二者皆無，而寒濕之痰，正賴溫以行之。"},{"t":"Reducing method, to clear the phlegm","c":"瀉法，以去其痰","ok":0,"note":"The phlegm is real, but it is the product of weakness, not of a strong pathogen. Draining a patient this empty removes the little she has and the phlegm returns. 痰誠有之，然為虛之所生，非強邪之所致。虛甚而瀉之，奪其僅存而痰復如故。"},{"t":"Drain the Lung points and reinforce the Spleen points","c":"肺穴用瀉，脾穴用補","ok":0,"note":"That was yesterday's answer, for a case with one full organ and one empty one. Today both organs are empty — there is nothing here to drain. 此昨日之法，為一實一虛而設。今二臟俱虛，無可瀉者。"}]};
